WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:02.490
- I love this too, that
your latest single,

00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:03.600
it's with your dad, right?

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:04.433
- [Noah] It is, yeah.

00:00:04.433 --> 00:00:05.400
- [Kelly] And it's "Noah Stand Still."

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:06.233
- [Noah] It is.

00:00:06.233 --> 00:00:07.290
- So, where does that come,

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:09.060
is it from him telling you to be still?

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:11.760
- Yeah, so I have stand
still here on my arm

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:12.593
and so does my dad.

00:00:12.593 --> 00:00:14.040
I'm actually covering my pinky

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:18.022
because I have all of
these nails, but one, so-

00:00:18.022 --> 00:00:19.783
- Oh, I've done that on this show!

00:00:19.783 --> 00:00:23.690
- I'm just going like this
for the remainder of our...

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:26.010
- I've totally done that
with my ring finger one time

00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:26.910
and I was like, "I'm gonna look like

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:28.080
I'm flashing gang signs."

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:30.330
I'm like, 'cause I was trying to hide it.

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:32.340
I didn't even notice, you're so good.

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:33.810
I was looking at your
cool tat so you're good.

00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:34.643
- Oh, thank you.

00:00:34.643 --> 00:00:37.980
So, no, stand still's just
been around through generations

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:39.340
on my dad's side.

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:43.920
His grandfather, his
dad, passed down to him

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:46.890
and has kind of shared that advice of,

00:00:46.890 --> 00:00:49.740
when you don't know what
to do, just stand still.

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:54.740
I took a trip to see my dad,
I think around August, 2020,

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:58.260
which was a couple months before I really

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:00.333
committed to recovery,

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:05.160
and we stood up on his hill in Nashville,

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:07.410
and Nashville's just
such a peaceful place.

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:08.340
- Beautiful, too, yeah.

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:10.350
- And he had me take my shoes off

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:11.850
and put my feet in the grass

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:13.590
and really get connected to home.

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:15.360
And he said, "Now we just stand still.

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:17.160
Like, breathe in the
air, just stand still,

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:19.740
and get connected back
to who you really are."

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:22.590
Like, you know, "None of
the rest of this matters.

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:24.570
Like, let's just be here, me and you."

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:26.550
And we had such an amazing moment

00:01:26.550 --> 00:01:29.430
that I hadn't had in such a long time

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:33.180
and he has no idea,
well, I mean, he will now

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:34.230
'cause he's watching this at home.

00:01:34.230 --> 00:01:35.063
Hi, Dad.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:40.923
But he really had no
idea, I think at the time.

00:01:40.923 --> 00:01:41.756
- [Kelly] The impact.

00:01:41.756 --> 00:01:42.803
- I think, as parents,

00:01:42.803 --> 00:01:44.653
you can see your child is struggling,

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:48.420
but he didn't know really
how much I really needed

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:50.790
to hear that and be reminded
of that at that time.

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:52.590
- That's so cool that you're able to like

00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:53.730
have that in your family.

00:01:53.730 --> 00:01:54.960
Y'all are musical and you have that gift

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:56.670
to be able to share together,
that's really special.

00:01:56.670 --> 00:02:00.840
I challenge everyone to find
something that's just artistic

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:02.970
'cause it comes out in a different way

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:04.773
and it's a good release, I think.

